---
import Presentation from "../../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import TargetImage from "../../../../assets/courses/ap-csp/img/lab-2-11-target.png";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Figure1 = `function drawBar(index, x) {
  let h = values[index] * 2.5;
  fill(80, 100, 140);
  rect(x, 320 - h, 38, h);
}`;

const Figure2 = `if (index === found) {
  fill(60, 200, 110);      // green: this is the one
} else if (index === current) {
  fill(240, 190, 60);      // yellow: checking it now
} else {
  fill(80, 100, 140);      // blue: not looked at
}`;

const Task1 = `let values = [42, 17, 93, 8, 55, 31, 76, 24];

function setup() {
  createCanvas(400, 400);
  textAlign(CENTER, CENTER);
  textSize(14);
  noStroke();

  background(20, 30, 50);

  for (let i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
    drawBar(i, 20 + i * 46);
  }
}

function drawBar(index, x) {
  let h = values[index] * 2.5;
  fill(80, 100, 140);
  rect(x, 320 - h, 38, h);
  fill(230);
  text(values[index], x + 19, 335);
}
`;

const Task2 = `let values = [42, 17, 93, 8, 55, 31, 76, 24];
let target = 55;
let current = -1;
let found = -1;

function setup() {
  createCanvas(400, 400);
  textAlign(CENTER, CENTER);
  textSize(14);
  noStroke();
}

function draw() {
  background(20, 30, 50);

  for (let i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
    drawBar(i, 20 + i * 46);
  }

  fill(230);
  text("Looking for " + target, 200, 30);

  if (found >= 0) {
    text("Found at index " + found, 200, 370);
  } else if (current >= values.length - 1) {
    text("Not in the list", 200, 370);
  } else {
    text("Click to check the next one", 200, 370);
  }
}

function drawBar(index, x) {
  let h = values[index] * 2.5;

  if (index === found) {
    fill(60, 200, 110);
  } else if (index === current) {
    fill(240, 190, 60);
  } else {
    fill(80, 100, 140);
  }

  rect(x, 320 - h, 38, h);
  fill(230);
  text(values[index], x + 19, 335);
}

function mousePressed() {
  if (found >= 0) {
    return;
  }

  current = current + 1;

  if (current < values.length && values[current] === target) {
    found = current;
  }
}
`;

const Task3 = `// Add a counter.
//   Show how many bars have been checked so far, on the canvas.
//
// Then change the target to a value that is NOT in the list,
//   and click all the way through.
//   The final count is the worst case you measured at 2.9.
//
// Then answer, in a comment on the canvas or in the code:
//   how many clicks would this take on a list of 800 bars?
`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Activity 2.11: p5 Lab 9 &mdash; Visualizing a Search</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- What You're Building -->
        <section id="target">
          <h2>What You're Building</h2>

          <div class="text-center my-4">
            <Image src={TargetImage} alt="Eight blue bars labeled with their values, with the bar for 55 highlighted in green and the caption Found at index 4" width={400} class="img-fluid rounded" />
          </div>

          <p>
            By the end of <b>Task 2</b>, each click checks the next bar. The bar
            being checked turns yellow; when the target is found it turns green
            and the search stops. This is five clicks in, looking for 55.
          </p>

          <p class="text-body-secondary">
            <b>Task 3 is not shown.</b> That one is yours to work out.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>p5 Lab 9</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Visualizing a Search</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Concepts</h2>
              <p>Data as a Picture</p>
              <p>One Step Per Click</p>
              <p>Watching the Worst Case</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>A List You Can See</h2>
              <Code code={Figure1} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="One Bar" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">Height comes from the value. Position comes from the index.</p>
              <p class="fragment">Two parameters, and between them they draw the whole list.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Color Carries the State</h2>
              <Code code={Figure2} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Three States" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">Not looked at. Looking now. Found.</p>
              <p class="fragment">The search has not changed. You can just see it.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>One Click, One Step</h2>
              <p>At 2.9 the loop ran to completion instantly.</p>
              <p class="fragment">Here <i>you</i> are the loop.</p>
              <p class="fragment">Each click does exactly one comparison.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>What That Buys You</h2>
              <p>The check count stops being a number in the output.</p>
              <p class="fragment">It becomes how many times you had to click.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today's Objectives</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Drawing a list as bars using a procedure with two parameters</li>
                <li>Using color to show the state of a search</li>
                <li>Advancing a linear search one comparison per click</li>
                <li>Measuring the worst case by clicking through it</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Terms</h2>
              <div class="text-start">
                <dl>
                  <dt>Visualization</dt>
                  <dd>A picture of data or a process that makes its shape visible.</dd>
                  <dt>State</dt>
                  <dd>What the program currently knows &mdash; here, which bar it is on and whether it has found the target.</dd>
                </dl>
              </div>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <p>
            Create a new <b>p5.js sketch</b> named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">2-11-search</b>.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 1: The List as Bars</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Create the sketch below and run it.</li>
            <li>
              Change one value in <code>values</code> and run it again. Only one
              bar should move.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>In a comment:</b> <code>drawBar</code> takes two parameters.
              Which one decides the height, and which decides the position?
            </li>
          </ul>
          <Code code={Task1} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="p5 Lab 9" class="mt-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 2: One Click, One Check</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Replace it with the version below and run it. Click through the search.</li>
            <li>Count your clicks. It should take five to find 55.</li>
            <li>
              Change <code>target</code> to <code>24</code> and click through
              again. <b>Record how many clicks that took.</b>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <Code code={Task2} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="p5 Lab 9" class="mt-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 3: Count the Worst Case</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Fill in the comment block.</li>
          </ul>
          <Code code={Task3} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="p5 Lab 9" class="mt-3" />

          <h5 class="mt-4">Challenge (optional)</h5>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Make the bars that have already been ruled out fade to a darker
              color instead of staying blue. Then say what that fading is showing
              you that the yellow bar alone does not.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>
            Clicking should advance the search exactly one bar at a time, the
            current bar should be visibly different from the rest, and the search
            should stop once the target is found.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Then answer this before you submit:</b> your sketch found 55 in
            five clicks. On a list of 800 bars, how many clicks would the worst
            case take? You do not need to build it &mdash; you need to know why
            the answer is 800.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer these before submitting your work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>The search logic here is the same as 2.9. What did seeing it change about your understanding of it, if anything? An honest "nothing" is a fine answer if you can say why.</li>
            <li>This sketch cannot visualize binary search without one change to the data. What is it?</li>
            <li><code>mousePressed()</code> advances the search, and <code>drawBar()</code> draws it. Only one of those two counts as a student-developed procedure. Which one, and why?</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Submit the required files to the appropriate dropbox.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Activity Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
